10. Additional Conditions: GodMode Cloud and Platform Commerce.

    The grants in Sections 2 and 3 are subject to all of the following.
    If You violate this Section 10, Your rights under this License
    terminate automatically.

    (a) No Competing Hosted Cloud. You may not use the Work or
        Derivative Works to offer, operate, sell, or rent a hosted
        multi-tenant (or invite-only multi-tenant) service that
        competes with GodMode Cloud, including a rebranded "BobMode
        Cloud" or similar, whether signup is public or gated, for
        seats, Marketplace paid checkout, Seller Connect, or
        GodMode Inference pack sales.

    (b) Private Hub allowed (no hosting resale). You may self-host and
        operate a Private Hub for Yourself or Your Legal Entity's
        internal use, provided You comply with Sections 10(c) and
        10(d). You may not sell, rent, or otherwise provide hosted
        access to the Work or Derivative Works to third-party customers
        as a competing Cloud-like service. Charging for Your own
        consulting, custom development, plugins, or on-prem support
        that is not hosted GodMode access remains allowed.

    (c) Keep Platform Commerce Features. In any distribution,
        deployment, or Derivative Work that includes a user-facing
        GodMode product surface (Local install, Private Hub, or
        similar), You must preserve Platform Commerce Features so
        that end users retain access to:
        (i)  the Official GodMode Marketplace catalog and Marketplace
             UI entry points shipped in Core; and
        (ii) the default Cloud commerce handoff to GodMode Cloud
             (or the Licensor's designated successor host) for paid
             Official and Community Marketplace checkout, Seller
             Connect, and GodMode Inference packs,
        unless the Licensor gives prior written permission to change
        those defaults.

    (d) No stripping or redirecting Core commerce. You may not remove,
        disable, obscure, or replace Platform Commerce Features in a
        way that blocks end users from Official Marketplace access or
        that redirects Core paid Marketplace, Seller Connect, or
        GodMode Inference pack checkout away from GodMode Cloud (or
        the Licensor's designated successor) to Your own payment
        rails, catalogs, or competing marketplace, except with the
        Licensor's prior written permission.

    (e) Allowed product work. Subject to this Section 10, You may
        rename Your fork for non-trademark-confusing use, add Core
        features, ship plugins, and build businesses that do not
        violate 10(a) through 10(d).

